    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1002" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγχῐ</span></b> , Poet. Adv. of place, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>near</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.185
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.449
			</span></i>, etc.:—freq. c. gen., which sts. precedes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἕκτορος ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.117
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.370
			</span></i>; but usu. follows, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. νεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.161
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πελαγίας ἁλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					467
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πλευμόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					639
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. γῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					399
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of Time, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. γὰρ ἀμέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					19.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			resemblance, <i>like</i>, c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				6.9
			</span></i>.—For 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσσον, ἄγχιστος</span>
			.</div>
